# **🔀 Open Redirect Vulnerability — CTF & Bug Bounty Notes**

## **1. What is Open Redirect?**

An **Open Redirect** occurs when a website redirects users to an external, attacker-controlled website without properly validating the destination URL.

**Example:**

```
https://example.com/login?redirect=https://attacker.com
```

The trusted website redirects the victim to `attacker.com`.

## **2. Attack flow diagram**

**👤 Victim**

Clicks a trusted-looking link

**🌐 Legitimate Website**

`example.com/login?redirect=...`

**⚠️ Weak URL Validation**

Accepts external destination

**💀 Attacker Website**

`attacker.com`

Phishing / credential theft

## **3. Types of Open Redirect**

| Type            | Description                           |
| --------------- | ------------------------------------- |
| Parameter-based | Redirect controlled by URL parameter  |
| Referer-based   | Redirect based on HTTP Referer header |

**Parameter-based example:**

```
/login?next=https://attacker.com
/login?redirect=https://attacker.com
```

**Referer-based flow:**

```
Attacker's webpage
       |
       v
Victim clicks legitimate login link
       |
       v
Browser sends Referer header
       |
       v
Website redirects to Referer URL
```

